The first implementation is in place and verifies across all four presets. A useful correction emerged from measuring rather than estimating: ordinary elimination exploits zeros created during row reduction and costs about 15,000 field operations at \(k=64\), not the dense worst-case count I initially projected. That is still roughly 57× the 262-operation compact route, but I’m correcting the Track B claim before running the gates.
