While auditing the canonicalization claim, I found a stronger native symmetry that needed coverage: an invertible change of basis in the module’s top summand. I’m strengthening the key to the exact row-reduced invariant (the multiset of the unique exponent residues), and adding elementary basis changes to G8. This avoids treating two coordinate presentations of the same module equation as distinct.
