"""Native S-unit equations over finite modules for arXiv:2505.19141.

The paper studies equations in which Laurent monomials act on elements of a
finitely presented module.  Here the module is M = F_p^k + F_p^k and the one
Laurent generator X acts by a square-zero shear

    X(a, b) = (a + U b, b).

For the standard bottom-basis vectors m_i, the equation
sum_i X**z_i m_i = (t, 1) is exactly U z = t modulo p.  The generator samples
z first and constructs t, so it never solves a generated instance.  U is a
dense wrapped-geometric circulant.  Generic modular Gaussian elimination is
