codex
One more hardening issue surfaced: after exhausting the fixed-length modulus increases, `escalate()` jumped to \(n=96\), where the intended shortcut costs 408 operations and violates G9’s 300-operation cap. I’m capping the final size increase at \(n=69\) (exactly 300 operations) and returning `cap_bound` thereafter, so the harness cannot misclassify an output-format limit as mathematical easiness.
apply patch
